<h1>About zoteamo</h1>
<p class="lede">zoteamo keeps one shared reading list for a reading group. Paste a link, DOI, ISBN, PubMed ID or arXiv ID, and it looks up the details and writes the citation for you.</p>

<h2>How the links work</h2>
<p>Each list has two secret links. The <strong>edit link</strong> lets anyone who has it add, change, vote on and delete items, so keep it within the group. The <strong>view link</strong> only shows the list and its exports, so you can share it more widely. Anyone with the edit link can replace it with a new one, which stops the old one working.</p>

<h2>Privacy</h2>
<p>There are no accounts, no analytics and no third-party requests. Lists are hidden from search engines. zoteamo sets three cookies, all on this site only:</p>
<ul>
  <li><code>zoteamo_voter</code>: a random ID so your votes count once.</li>
  <li><code>zoteamo_name</code>: the name you last added items under, to fill in the form for you.</li>
  <li><code>zoteamo_style</code>: the citation style you last chose.</li>
</ul>

